<title>INDIA: India's PNB cuts prime lending rate by 1.0 pct.</title>
<headline>India's PNB cuts prime lending rate by 1.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Punjab National Bank on Thursday reduced its prime lending rate by one percentage point to 15 percent, its chairman said.  </p>
<p>PNB's chairman Rashid Jilani told Reuters that the lower rate would be effective from Friday, November 1.</p>
<p>United News of India (UNI) said the bank has decided to keep the maximum spread over the lending rate at four percent on various types of advances except for consumer credit.</p>
<p>--New Delhi newsroom +91-11-301 2024</p>
</text>
